n weapon  with fire but uses a super soaker with  gas in it that was really cool to watch  but by the end of all this when we're  back at the police station she's talking  to them more this movie started  the key here is that she told them that  kevin james's crew was looking for a  canadian quarter she does not mention  this key that is on her neck  that has the white supremacist symbol on  it so i  really wonder again where are they  teasing you with becky here is she  becoming a white nationalist or she just  a crazy person or you could think so  many things here maybe she just takes it  as  a token of memory of that the time she  survived all these people  and prospered maybe that's just all teas  so  it's interesting it makes you think it's  a really fun watch  and i really love it just went balls to  the walls i thought lula wilson did  amazing  and i thought kevin james was pretty  good you know i think that  it wasn't one of those roles that it  kind of it's not that challenging it's  not showing you what he can really do  yet as a dramatic actor but i think it  has a lot of promise for him  i think he did good with what he was  given and i think there was just a lot  of good comedic writing in here it was  subtle  didn't take away from all the other  important aspects of the drama and the  motion to the film  and again great score it served its  purpose  and i think that watching it the second  time  i enjoyed it more you appreciate it more  knowing where it ends up  and seeing becky's transformation as the  film goes on and  i think that was the most effective part  how they lined it up with apex's  transformation where he was  becoming less of a killer so to me this  gets an 8.7  let me know what you thought down below  i'd love to hear your thoughts  i read every comment and try to respond  as many as i can please make sure to  check out my review of shirley that also  came out this weekend with elizabeth  moss i think you'll be interested to  hear my th